### Proposals API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for proposal management endpoints
### All operations for creating, reading, updating, and managing proposals
### Reviewed and verified against implementation

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@freelancerToken = your-freelancer-jwt-token-here
@clientToken = your-client-jwt-token-here
@proposalId = your-proposal-uuid-here
@projectId = your-project-uuid-here
@userId = your-user-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp
### - @freelancerToken: JWT token for a freelancer user
### - @clientToken: JWT token for a client user (for favorite toggle)
### - @proposalId: UUID of an existing proposal
### - @projectId: UUID of an existing project
### - @userId: UUID of an existing user

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE PROPOSAL
### ============================================
### Create a new proposal for a project (requires authentication and freelancer role)
### Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
### Required fields: projectId, description, budget, duration, files
### Cannot create proposal for your own project
### Cannot create proposal if project is not open for bids
### Cannot create duplicate proposal for the same project
### Files are REQUIRED (at least one file must be provided)

POST {{baseUrl}}/proposals
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "description": "I can complete this project efficiently. I have 5+ years of experience in React and Node.js development. I will deliver high-quality code with proper testing and documentation.",
  "budget": 3500.50,
  "duration": 20,
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440003",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "proposal"
    }
  ]
}

### Create Proposal with Multiple Files
POST {{baseUrl}}/proposals
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "description": "I have extensive experience in full-stack development. My portfolio includes similar projects that I've successfully completed. I'm confident I can deliver this project on time and within budget.",
  "budget": 4500.00,
  "duration": 25,
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440003",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "proposal"
    },
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440004",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "proposal"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================
### 2. GET PROPOSAL BY ID (PUBLIC)
### ============================================
### Get a specific proposal by its ID
### No authentication required - Public access
### Returns proposal with filesData array containing file URLs and metadata

GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example with actual UUID:
GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ============================================
### 3. GET PROPOSALS BY PROJECT ID (PUBLIC)
### ============================================
### Get all proposals for a specific project
### No authentication required - Public access
### Useful for project owners to see all proposals submitted for their project
### Returns array of proposals with filesData

GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/project/{{projectId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example with actual UUID:
GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/project/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ============================================
### 4. GET PROPOSALS BY USER ID (PUBLIC)
### ============================================
### Get all proposals submitted by a specific user
### No authentication required - Public access
### Useful for freelancers to see all their submitted proposals
### Returns array of proposals with filesData

GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/user/{{userId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Example with actual UUID:
GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/user/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### ============================================
### 5. UPDATE PROPOSAL (EDIT PROPOSAL)
### ============================================
### Update/Edit a proposal (requires authentication and freelancer role)
### Only the proposal creator can update their proposal
### At least one field must be provided
### Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
### All fields are optional - update only what you need

### Update Multiple Fields (Comprehensive Example)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "description": "Updated proposal description with more details about my approach and qualifications.",
  "budget": 3800.00,
  "duration": 22,
  "status": "pending",
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440005",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "proposal"
    }
  ]
}

### Update Only Description
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "description": "Updated proposal description with revised approach and additional qualifications."
}

### Update Only Budget
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "budget": 4000.00
}

### Update Only Duration
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "duration": 25
}

### Update Budget and Duration Together
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "budget": 4200.00,
  "duration": 28
}

### Update Status
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "status": "accepted"
}

### Update Files Only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "files": [
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440006",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "proposal"
    },
    {
      "fileId": "770e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-446655440007",
      "token": "upload-token-from-s3-upload-url-endpoint",
      "purpose": "proposal"
    }
  ]
}

### Update Description and Budget Together
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

{
  "description": "Revised proposal with updated budget and timeline.",
  "budget": 4500.00
}

### ============================================
### 6. TOGGLE FAVORITE PROPOSAL
### ============================================
### Toggle the favorite status of a proposal (requires authentication)
### Can be used by project owners to mark proposals as favorites
### Toggles between true and false
### No request body required
### Any authenticated user can toggle favorite (not restricted to project owner)

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}/favorite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Example with actual UUID:
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000/favorite
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================
### 7. DELETE PROPOSAL
### ============================================
### Delete a proposal (requires authentication and freelancer role)
### Only the proposal creator can delete their proposal
### This is a permanent deletion - cannot be undone
### Note: Service layer doesn't check ownership - deletion is allowed for any freelancer
### Consider adding ownership validation in the service layer

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

### Example with actual UUID:
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/proposals/123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{freelancerToken}}

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Most endpoints require JWT token in Authorization header
###    - Format: Authorization: Bearer <token>
###    - Get token from: POST /api/auth/verify-otp
###    
###    Public endpoints (no auth required):
###    - GET /api/proposals/:id (get proposal by ID)
###    - GET /api/proposals/project/:projectId (get proposals by project)
###    - GET /api/proposals/user/:userId (get proposals by user)
###    
###    Freelancer-only endpoints (requires freelancer role):
###    - POST /api/proposals (create proposal)
###    - PATCH /api/proposals/:id (update/edit proposal)
###    - DELETE /api/proposals/:id (delete proposal)
###    
###    User endpoints (requires authentication, any role):
###    - PATCH /api/proposals/:id/favorite (toggle favorite)

### 2. FILE UPLOADS
###    - Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
###    - File purpose must be "proposal" for proposal files
###    - File format: [{ fileId: "uuid", token: "upload-token", purpose: "proposal" }]
###    - Files must be uploaded to S3 before they can be used in proposal creation/update
###    - Files are REQUIRED when creating a proposal (validation enforces this)
###    - Files are optional when updating a proposal
###    - Upload flow:
###      1. POST /api/s3/upload-url with filePurpose: "proposal"
###      2. Upload file to S3 using the returned uploadUrl
###      3. Use fileId and token in proposal creation/update request
###    - Files are stored as array of UUIDs in the database
###    - filesData is automatically attached to responses with file URLs and metadata

### 3. PROPOSAL STATUS VALUES
###    - "pending" - Proposal is pending review (default)
###    - "accepted" - Proposal has been accepted by project owner
###    - "rejected" - Proposal has been rejected by project owner
###    - Status can be updated by the proposal creator (freelancer)
###    - Status is typically managed by project owner through contracts/acceptance flow

### 4. BUDGET VALIDATION
###    - Budget must be a positive number
###    - Budget is stored as DECIMAL(10, 2) (supports 2 decimal places)
###    - Budget represents the proposed amount for completing the project
###    - Example: 3500.50, 4500.00

### 5. DURATION VALIDATION
###    - Duration must be a positive integer
###    - Duration represents the number of days to complete the project
###    - Must be greater than 0
###    - Example: 14, 20, 30

### 6. DESCRIPTION VALIDATION
###    - Description is required when creating a proposal
###    - Description must be between 1 and 500 characters
###    - Description should explain the freelancer's approach and qualifications
###    - Trimmed automatically (leading/trailing whitespace removed)

### 7. PROPOSAL CREATION RULES
###    - Cannot create proposal for your own project (validated in service)
###    - Cannot create proposal if project status is not "openforbids" (validated in service)
###    - Cannot create duplicate proposal (one proposal per user per project, validated in service)
###    - Project must exist and be active (validated in service)
###    - User must be a freelancer (validated by Freelancer middleware)
###    - Files are required (validated by Joi schema)
###    - User must be active (non-deleted, validated by model hook)

### 8. UPDATE PROPOSAL (EDIT PROPOSAL)
###    - Endpoint: PATCH /api/proposals/:id
###    - Only the proposal creator can update their proposal (note: service doesn't check ownership currently)
###    - At least one field must be provided (validated by Joi schema)
###    - All fields are optional - you can update any combination of fields
###    - Editable fields:
###      * description: String (1-500 characters)
###      * budget: Positive number (2 decimal places)
###      * duration: Positive integer (in days)
###      * status: Enum (pending, accepted, rejected)
###      * files: Array of file references with upload tokens
###    - Files can be updated by providing new file references
###    - Files require upload tokens from /api/s3/upload-url endpoint first
###    - Status can be updated (though typically managed by project owner)
###    - Returns 404 Not Found if proposal doesn't exist
###    - Note: Consider adding ownership validation in service layer

### 9. FAVORITE PROPOSAL
###    - FavoriteProposal is a boolean field
###    - Used by project owners to mark proposals they're interested in
###    - Can be toggled on/off by any authenticated user
###    - Default value is false
###    - Toggles between true and false on each call
###    - No request body required

### 10. DELETE PROPOSAL
###     - Endpoint: DELETE /api/proposals/:id
###     - Requires authentication and freelancer role
###     - Permanent deletion (force: true)
###     - Returns 404 Not Found if proposal doesn't exist
###     - Note: Service doesn't check ownership - any freelancer can delete any proposal
###     - Consider adding ownership validation in service layer

### 11. REQUIRED FIELDS FOR CREATE
###     - projectId: UUID (required, must exist in Projects table)
###     - description: String (1-500 characters, required)
###     - budget: Positive number (required, 2 decimal places)
###     - duration: Positive integer (required, in days)
###     - files: Array of file references (required, at least one file)
###     - Files format: [{ fileId: "uuid", token: "upload-token", purpose: "proposal" }]

### 12. OPTIONAL FIELDS FOR UPDATE
###     - description: String (1-500 characters, optional)
###     - budget: Positive number (optional, 2 decimal places)
###     - duration: Positive integer (optional, in days)
###     - status: Enum (pending, accepted, rejected, optional)
###     - files: Array of file references (optional)
###     - At least one field must be provided when updating

### 13. ERROR RESPONSES
###     - 400 Bad Request: Invalid input data, validation errors, duplicate proposal
###     - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid authentication token
###     - 403 Forbidden: User doesn't have required role (freelancer) or trying to create proposal for own project
###     - 404 Not Found: Proposal, project, or user not found
###     - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error

### 14. FILE REFERENCE FORMAT
###     - Single file: [{ fileId: "uuid", token: "upload-token", purpose: "proposal" }]
###     - Multiple files: Array of file objects
###     - Files must be uploaded to S3 first using /api/s3/upload-url
###     - Upload token must match the fileId and purpose
###     - Files are stored as array of UUIDs in database
###     - filesData is automatically populated in responses with full file information

### 15. RESPONSE DATA STRUCTURE
###     - All GET endpoints return proposals with filesData array
###     - filesData contains: id, url, fileName, fileType, filePurpose, mimeType, fileSize, status, createdAt, updatedAt
###     - Proposal response includes:
###       * id: UUID
###       * projectId: UUID
###       * userId: UUID (freelancer who created the proposal)
###       * description: String
###       * budget: Decimal
###       * duration: Integer
###       * status: Enum (pending, accepted, rejected)
###       * FavoriteProposal: Boolean
###       * files: Array of UUIDs
###       * filesData: Array of file objects with URLs
###       * createdAt: Timestamp

### 16. EXAMPLE WORKFLOW
###     1. Authenticate: POST /api/auth/verify-otp (get token)
###     2. Get upload URL: POST /api/s3/upload-url (filePurpose: "proposal")
###     3. Upload file to S3 using uploadUrl
###     4. Create proposal: POST /api/proposals (with fileId and token)
###     5. View proposal: GET /api/proposals/:id
###     6. View all proposals for project: GET /api/proposals/project/:projectId
###     7. Edit/Update proposal: PATCH /api/proposals/:id
###        - Update budget: { "budget": 4000.00 }
###        - Update duration: { "duration": 25 }
###        - Update multiple fields: { "budget": 4000, "duration": 25, "description": "..." }
###     8. Toggle favorite: PATCH /api/proposals/:id/favorite
###     9. Delete proposal: DELETE /api/proposals/:id

### 17. BUSINESS RULES
###     - A freelancer can only submit one proposal per project (enforced in service)
###     - Proposals can only be created for projects with status "openforbids" (enforced in service)
###     - Project owners cannot create proposals for their own projects (enforced in service)
###     - Proposal status can be updated by freelancer (pending, accepted, rejected)
###     - Favorite proposals are highlighted for project owners
###     - Files are required to provide supporting documents/portfolio
###     - User must be active (non-deleted) to create proposal (enforced by model hook)

### 18. DATA RELATIONSHIPS
###     - Proposals belong to a Project (projectId, foreign key to Projects table)
###     - Proposals are created by a User (userId, foreign key to Users table, must be freelancer)
###     - Proposals can have multiple Files (files array of UUIDs referencing FileHub table)
###     - filesData is populated from FileHub table with full file information
###     - Proposals have a status (pending, accepted, rejected)
###     - Proposals can be marked as favorite (FavoriteProposal boolean)
###     - Database indexes on: projectId, userId, status, FavoriteProposal, createdAt, (projectId, userId), (projectId, status), files (GIN index)

### 19. IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
###     - Service layer validates: project exists, not own project, project is open, no duplicate
###     - Repository pattern used for data access
###     - DTO pattern used for data transformation
###     - File attachment handled by middleware (validateUploadItems, confirmUploadMiddleware)
###     - Files are fetched in bulk and attached to proposals (optimized query)
###     - Error handling with proper status codes
###     - Model hooks validate user is active before proposal creation

### 20. BEST PRACTICES
###     - Include detailed description explaining your approach
###     - Provide realistic budget and duration estimates
###     - Attach relevant portfolio files or samples
###     - Update proposal if project requirements change
###     - Keep proposal description professional and clear
###     - Respond promptly to proposal status changes
###     - Use favorite feature to shortlist promising proposals

### 21. INTEGRATION NOTES
###     - Proposals are public (can be viewed without authentication)
###     - Only freelancers can create/update/delete proposals
###     - Project owners use favorite feature to shortlist proposals
###     - Proposal status changes may trigger notifications (if implemented)
###     - Files are stored in S3 and referenced by UUID
###     - File metadata is automatically included in responses

### 22. SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
###     - Authentication required for create/update/delete operations
###     - Freelancer role required for proposal management
###     - Project ownership validated before proposal creation
###     - Project status validated before proposal creation
###     - Duplicate proposal prevention
###     - File upload tokens validated before attachment
###     - User must be active (non-deleted) to create proposals

### 23. PERFORMANCE NOTES
###     - Files are fetched in bulk using single query (optimized)
###     - Database indexes on commonly queried fields
###     - GIN index on files array for efficient array queries
###     - Composite indexes for common query patterns